    "answer": {
      "short": "A",
      "worked": "Both ends point down, so the leading coefficient is negative. This eliminates B.\n\nThe $x$-intercepts are $-2,\\ \\tfrac12,\\ 2,\\ 3$, so the factors are $(x+2)$, $(2x-1)$, $(x-2)$, $(x-3)$. This eliminates C (it has $x=1$) and D (it has $x=-\\tfrac12$).\n\nCheck the $y$-intercept of A at $x=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-(2)(-1)(-2)(-3)\\\\y&=12\\end{align*}$$\nThis matches the graph, so the answer is A.",
